insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('73c02adc-a95f-5628-9262-fdf377c1ba7e', 'wg6-informative-writing-p06', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g6-informative-writing'), null,
        '6-8', $q$Bookmobiles: Libraries on Wheels$q$, $q$(1) A bookmobile is a vehicle that carries library books to people who live far from a library building. (2) Some bookmobiles are vans, and others are large buses with shelves built along the walls. (3) They visit schools, parks, senior centers and small towns on a regular schedule.

(4) Bookmobiles solve an important problem. (5) In many rural areas, the nearest library may be an hour's drive away. (6) Families without cars, older adults and young children may not be able to make that trip. (7) A bookmobile brings the library to them, often stopping in the same spot every week or two.

(8) Today's bookmobiles offer more than books. (9) Many carry laptops and wireless internet so visitors can search for jobs or finish homework. (10) Some have puzzles, games and audiobooks. (11) Librarians on board can also help people sign up for library cards.

(12) Bookmobiles show that a library is more than a building.$q$, 'draft')
