   $q$Read the sentence from a lab report: "We measured the temperature of the water every five minutes, and it got super hot really fast." Which revision keeps the tone consistent?$q$, $q$[{"text":"We measured the temperature of the water every five minutes, and it rose rapidly.","is_correct":true},{"text":"We measured the temperature of the water every five minutes, and it kind of rose sort of fast.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"vague-hedging"},{"text":"We measured the temperature of the water every five minutes, and whoa, it heated up.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"informal-interjection"},{"text":"We measured the temperature of the water every five minutes, and it got crazy hot fast.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"informal-word"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$We measured the temperature of the water every five minutes, and it rose rapidly.$q$, $q$"Rose rapidly" matches the careful, formal start of the sentence. "Kind of" and "sort of" avoid slang but still sound casual and make the result vague.$q$, 'draft', null)
