   $q$A student is writing a letter to the principal asking for a longer lunch period. Which sentence best keeps a respectful, formal tone?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A longer lunch period would give students time to eat without rushing.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Lunch is way too short and everybody totally hates it.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"informal-exaggeration"},{"text":"Make lunch longer right away or we will all complain.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"demanding-tone"},{"text":"You obviously do not care how hungry all of us get.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"disrespectful-tone"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A longer lunch period would give students time to eat without rushing.$q$, $q$This sentence gives a clear reason in calm, polite words. "You obviously do not care how hungry all of us get" avoids slang, but it blames the principal, which is disrespectful.$q$, 'draft', null)
