   $q$The art club counted $312 at the end of its bake sale. A student wrote for the school paper: "The bake sale made like a million dollars!" Which revision is the most precise and fits a news article?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The bake sale made like $312!","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"informal-filler"},{"text":"The bake sale raised about a million dollars.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"inaccurate-exaggeration"},{"text":"The bake sale raised $312.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The bake sale raised a ton of money.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"vague-amount"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The bake sale raised $312.$q$, $q$A news article should give the exact amount in plain words, and the club counted $312. "Made like $312!" has the right number but keeps the casual "like" and the exclamation.$q$, 'draft', null)
