   $q$A bean plant was 4 centimeters tall on Monday and 10 centimeters tall two weeks later. A student wrote: "The bean plant grew a lot in two weeks." Which revision is the most precise?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The bean plant grew 6 centimeters in two weeks.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The bean plant grew 10 centimeters in two weeks.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-data"},{"text":"The bean plant grew hugely in two weeks.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"vague-amount"},{"text":"The bean plant grew a bunch in two weeks.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"vague-amount"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The bean plant grew 6 centimeters in two weeks.$q$, $q$The plant went from 4 to 10 centimeters, so it grew exactly 6 centimeters. "10 centimeters" is precise but wrong, because that is the final height, not the growth.$q$, 'draft', null)
