   $q$Read the sentence from a flyer for a school book sale: "Our used books are cheap." The writer wants the books to sound like a good deal, not poor quality. Which word should replace "cheap"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"flimsy","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"negative-connotation"},{"text":"worthless","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"negative-connotation"},{"text":"costly","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"affordable","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$affordable$q$, $q$"Affordable" means low in price without suggesting the books are badly made. "Flimsy" and "worthless" make the books sound poor, which is the feeling the writer wants to avoid.$q$, 'draft', null)
