   $q$Read the paragraph from a report about an ancient city: "The city of Velmora, built along a river, was a busy trading center. Merchants sold cloth, grain, and pottery in its markets. The markets were basically the coolest hangout spots ever. Visitors arrived by boat from distant towns." Which revision of the third sentence best matches the tone of the paragraph?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The markets were the liveliest gathering places in the city.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The markets were, without a doubt, the most amazing places in all of history.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"exaggerated-tone"},{"text":"The markets were awesome places for people to hang out.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"informal-word"},{"text":"The markets were places.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"flat-wording"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The markets were the liveliest gathering places in the city.$q$, $q$"Liveliest gathering places" keeps the idea that the markets were popular, but in the same serious style as the rest of the report. "The most amazing places in all of history" avoids slang, but its huge claim does not fit a factual report.$q$, 'draft', null)
