        '6-8', $q$Draft: The Long Trip of the Monarchs$q$, $q$(1) In the article "A Long Trip on Thin Wings," Ayesha Rahman explains how monarch butterflies travel thousands of miles each fall. (2) ____. (3) Rahman writes that monarchs fly south to the same mountain forests every year, even though no single butterfly has made the trip before. (4) She explains that the butterflies use the position of the sun to keep flying in the right direction. (5) This detail shows that monarchs are born with a kind of built-in compass.

(6) Monarchs also need help from the land along the way. (7) Rahman reports that the butterflies stop to drink nectar from fall flowers so they have enough energy to keep going. (8) My grandmother has a painting of a purple butterfly in her kitchen. (9) Rahman notes that in areas where fields of wildflowers were replaced by parking lots, fewer monarchs were counted. (10) ____, the trip depends on flowers being there when the butterflies need them.

(11) Monarchs are pretty.$q$, 'draft')
