   $q$Which sentence best fills blank (4) to continue the evidence about how paper was made?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Bark is the tough outer layer of a tree that protects the wood inside.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-evidence"},{"text":"Paper is also made from old newspapers in many cities and towns today.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-topic-fact"},{"text":"Okafor thinks that handmade paper is much prettier than paper from a store.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Next, the workers pounded the soft fibers into pulp and spread thin layers of it on screens to dry.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Next, the workers pounded the soft fibers into pulp and spread thin layers of it on screens to dry.$q$, $q$Sentence 3 describes the first step, soaking, so the next step of making pulp and drying it continues the evidence about slow, careful work. The sentence about bark is true, but it does not come from Okafor's description of papermaking.$q$, 'draft', '29ffc352-e7dd-5e28-84ac-45689addf0a8')
