  ('b2dcc241-46db-510e-b27d-68fa43cac92f', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g6-writing-with-evidence'), null, 'easy',
   $q$Which sentence best fills blank (2) as the claim of the draft?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Mbeki says that one league counted how often its players touched the ball.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Soccer leagues for young players can be found in many towns and cities.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"topic-not-claim"},{"text":"Mbeki believes that full-size soccer fields should no longer be used by anyone.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Mbeki argues that smaller games help young players build skills faster because they practice more and think quickly.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Mbeki argues that smaller games help young players build skills faster because they practice more and think quickly.$q$, $q$The draft gives evidence about more touches in paragraph 1 and quicker thinking in paragraph 2, so the claim must cover both. The league that counted touches is only one piece of evidence, so it is too narrow to be the claim.$q$, 'draft', '9ddeec85-6a0e-54b0-b4a3-cb4c9f2dc948')
