insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('f4d5d3d9-ad53-55b1-a094-6a30d5e02f64', 'wg6-writing-with-evidence-p04', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g6-writing-with-evidence'), null,
        '6-8', $q$Draft: Messages from the Sky$q$, $q$(1) Daniel Kowalczyk's article "Messages from the Sky" describes how large balloons filled with gas are sent into the sky each day to help forecasters understand the weather. (2) Kowalczyk shows that weather balloons give forecasters information they could not easily get any other way. (3) He explains that each balloon carries a small box of sensors that measures temperature, wind, and moisture as it rises. (4) According to Kowalczyk, the balloons climb much higher than most airplanes fly. (5) ____.

(6) The information is also shared quickly. (7) Kowalczyk writes that the box sends its readings back to the ground by radio every second or two. (8) Forecasters then feed these numbers into computers that use them to predict the weather for the next several days. (9) My uncle once found a fallen sensor box in his field. (10) Because the readings arrive so fast, forecasters can warn people about storms sooner.$q$, 'draft')
