   $q$Which sentence best fills blank (4) with evidence that supports sentence 5?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Watanabe describes the strong suction cups an octopus uses to grip slippery rocks.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-evidence"},{"text":"Watanabe describes an octopus resting on sand that turned pale and speckled to match the ground.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Watanabe describes an octopus flashing dark stripes at another octopus nearby.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misplaced-evidence"},{"text":"Many people think that octopuses are the smartest animals in the whole sea.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opinion-not-evidence"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Watanabe describes an octopus resting on sand that turned pale and speckled to match the ground.$q$, $q$Sentence 5 says the detail shows hiding, and an octopus matching the sand is an example of hiding. The stripes example is from the article, but it shows communication, which is the point of paragraph 2.$q$, 'draft', '9d881e6d-8728-5251-b1f6-5e61a5904fe4')
