        '6-8', $q$Saving Birds at Crestview$q$, $q$(1) Last fall, students at Crestview Middle School found more than forty birds stunned or hurt below the windows of the new library wing. (2) ______ (3) Birds cannot see clear glass, so they fly straight toward the trees and sky reflected in it. (4) Scientists who study birds estimate that window strikes harm millions of birds in our country every year. (5) Small dot stickers placed about two inches apart break up the reflection and warn birds that something solid is there.

(6) Some teachers worry that the dots would block the view from the library. (7) However, the dots are small and spaced apart, so readers could still see outside clearly. (8) The science club tested a sample panel in October, and no student who sat near it said the view was harder to see. (9) Also, the stickers for the whole wing cost about two hundred dollars, which the club could raise at one bake sale. (10) Crestview's new building is the largest one in the district.

(11) A simple layer of dots would let Crestview keep its bright new library and protect the birds that share our campus.$q$, 'draft')
