   $q$Which piece of evidence would best support the response in sentence (8)?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Ultimate disc was first played by a group of high school students many years ago.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-history"},{"text":"Basketball is also hard to learn at first, especially dribbling with the weaker hand.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"shifts-focus"},{"text":"Some professional players can throw a disc more than seventy yards in a single toss.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"does-not-address-beginners"},{"text":"In a trial lesson last spring, 25 of 28 seventh graders completed five passes in a row by the end of class.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$In a trial lesson last spring, 25 of 28 seventh graders completed five passes in a row by the end of class.$q$, $q$Sentence (8) says beginners can make short passes after one class, and the trial lesson shows exactly that. The fact about professional players says nothing about how quickly beginners learn.$q$, 'draft', 'f792b05e-1f42-5786-bf89-4ef0adb08d11')
