   $q$Which sentence about the hikers is punctuated correctly?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The hikers rested under a large oak tree before the long difficult, climb.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-before-noun"},{"text":"The hikers rested under a large, oak tree before the long difficult climb.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"commas-reversed"},{"text":"The hikers rested under a large oak tree before the long, difficult climb.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The hikers rested under a large, oak tree before the long, difficult climb.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-cumulative-adjectives"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The hikers rested under a large oak tree before the long, difficult climb.$q$, $q$"Long" and "difficult" equally describe the climb, so they take a comma, but "oak tree" is a unit and "large and oak tree" sounds wrong. The choice with commas in both places wrongly treats "large oak" as coordinate adjectives.$q$, 'draft', null)
