   $q$Read the sentence: "Because the wind was too strong we moved the picnic indoors." Which revision is punctuated correctly?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Because the wind was too strong we moved, the picnic indoors.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-between-verb-object"},{"text":"Because, the wind was too strong we moved the picnic indoors.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-after-first-word"},{"text":"Because the wind was too strong; we moved the picnic indoors.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"semicolon-after-dependent-clause"},{"text":"Because the wind was too strong, we moved the picnic indoors.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Because the wind was too strong, we moved the picnic indoors.$q$, $q$The dependent clause "Because the wind was too strong" opens the sentence, so a comma marks where the main clause begins. A semicolon is wrong because it should join two complete clauses, and the "because" clause cannot stand alone.$q$, 'draft', null)
