   $q$Maya does two things in one sentence. Which version is punctuated correctly?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Maya opened, the seed packet and poured the seeds into the tray.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-between-verb-object"},{"text":"Maya opened the seed packet and poured the seeds into the tray.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Maya opened the seed packet, and poured the seeds into the tray.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-in-compound-predicate"},{"text":"Maya opened the seed packet and poured, the seeds into the tray.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-after-second-verb"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Maya opened the seed packet and poured the seeds into the tray.$q$, $q$The sentence has one subject, "Maya," with two verbs, so it is not two clauses and needs no comma before "and." The comma before "and" is tempting, but there is no second subject after "and" to start a new clause.$q$, 'draft', null)
