   $q$Read the sentence: "We spent a long quiet peaceful afternoon at the lake." Which revision is punctuated correctly?$q$, $q$[{"text":"We spent a long quiet, peaceful afternoon at the lake.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"missing-coordinate-comma"},{"text":"We spent a, long, quiet, peaceful afternoon at the lake.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-after-article"},{"text":"We spent a long, quiet, peaceful, afternoon at the lake.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-before-noun"},{"text":"We spent a long, quiet, peaceful afternoon at the lake.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$We spent a long, quiet, peaceful afternoon at the lake.$q$, $q$All three adjectives describe the afternoon equally, so a comma separates each pair, but no comma comes before the noun. The choice with a comma after "peaceful" wrongly cuts off the noun "afternoon."$q$, 'draft', null)
