-- Passage wg7-informative-writing-p05
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('bfa056b4-49f1-52b7-8ddf-7d4e47a49419', 'wg7-informative-writing-p05', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g7-informative-writing'), null,
        '6-8', $q$Wheelchair Basketball$q$, $q$(1) Wheelchair basketball is a fast team sport played by athletes who have physical disabilities. (2) The game follows most of the same rules as standard basketball. (3) The court is the same size, and the hoop is the same height of ten feet. (4) Each team has five players on the court, and points are scored the same way.

(5) A few rules are changed to fit the wheelchair. (6) In standard basketball, a player who takes too many steps without dribbling is called for traveling. (7) In wheelchair basketball, a player may push the wheels twice, but then must dribble, pass, or shoot. (8) Players also use special sports chairs. (9) These chairs have wheels that slant inward, which makes them more stable during sharp turns.

(10) Many leagues use a classification system to keep teams fair. (11) Each player receives a point value based on how much movement he or she has in the trunk and legs. (12) Players with less movement receive lower numbers. (13) The point values of a team's five players on the court cannot add up to more than a set total. (14) Therefore, every team must include athletes with a range of abilities.

(15) Wheelchair basketball is played in schools, local clubs, and international competitions.$q$, 'draft')
