        '6-8', $q$The Pizza Box Oven$q$, $q$(1) Our science teacher, Ms. Adeyemi, gave every pair of students the same challenge: build an oven that could melt chocolate using only sunlight. (2) My partner Tomas and I lined a pizza box with foil and taped plastic wrap over a window in the lid. (3) We set our oven on the blacktop at ten o'clock and placed a square of chocolate inside. (4) Then we waited. (5) After twenty minutes, the chocolate looked exactly the same. (6) Tomas poked the plastic wrap and sighed. (7) Other groups were already cheering as their chocolate turned glossy and soft. (8) Chocolate is made from the seeds of the cacao tree. (9) I knelt down beside our box and noticed that its shadow stretched out to the left. (10) The sun had moved, and our foil flap was no longer catching the light.

(11) "We have to aim it again," I said. (12) We tilted the box and propped the flap with a ruler so the foil reflected sunlight straight through the window. (13) Every few minutes we checked the shadow and turned the box a little more. (14) Just before the bell, Tomas lifted the lid. (15) The chocolate had slumped into a shiny puddle.

(16) The experiment was over.$q$, 'draft')
