   $q$Which sentence would best replace sentence 14 as a conclusion that connects back to the beginning of the narrative?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Then I went upstairs and started typing up my history project on the computer.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"flat-ending-no-reflection"},{"text":"As I closed my notebook, I realized her \"room full of wires\" had really been a room full of people.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Telephones have changed a great deal since the 1960s, and they will keep changing.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"generic-fact-ending"},{"text":"Nana Rose was a telephone operator who worked in a room with many wires.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"restates-situation"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$As I closed my notebook, I realized her "room full of wires" had really been a room full of people.$q$, $q$The correct choice echoes the phrase from sentence 2 and shows what the narrator now understands about the job. The choice about Nana Rose being an operator only repeats the situation without any new insight.$q$, 'draft', 'd1d1d39c-d039-54a2-a4e7-525c97637e8f')
