-- Passage wg7-narrative-writing-p04
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('30ffdc0e-3d8d-5c9c-beba-8d0ce8ee1dc7', 'wg7-narrative-writing-p04', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g7-narrative-writing'), null,
        '6-8', $q$Counting in Fives$q$, $q$(1) At six in the morning, my aunt Marisol and I stood at the edge of Willow Marsh with binoculars, a clipboard, and two thermoses of cocoa. (2) We were volunteers for the winter bird count, which meant we had to record every bird we saw in one hour. (3) My breath made small clouds in the cold air. (4) For the first ten minutes, we saw nothing but brown reeds. (5) Then a flock of small gray birds with white bellies landed on the path. (6) "Juncos," Aunt Marisol whispered.

(7) I started counting, but they kept hopping around, and I lost track at fourteen. (8) Aunt Marisol showed me a trick. (9) Instead of counting single birds, I could count groups of five and multiply. (10) My binoculars were a birthday present from my uncle two years ago. (11) I tried again and counted six groups, which made thirty juncos. (12) We counted a heron, two cardinals, and a woodpecker. (13) When the hour ended, our list had eleven kinds of birds on it.

(14) Birds are fun.$q$, 'draft')
