insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('77381ee9-bc59-5c9c-9357-3a5d3b4561be', 'wg7-narrative-writing-p05', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g7-narrative-writing'), null,
        '6-8', $q$The Last Hill$q$, $q$(1) The Riverside cross-country course is famous for one thing: a steep hill right before the finish. (2) I had run the course twice in practice, and both times I had walked up that hill. (3) On the day of the league meet, Coach Benally pulled me aside before the start. (4) "Run your own race," she said. (5) "Save something for the hill."

(6) The starting horn blasted, and sixty runners surged across the grass. (7) I got caught up in the crowd and sprinted the first mile with the leaders. (8) By the second mile, my legs felt heavy and my side ached. (9) Our team bus is yellow with a blue stripe. (10) Then I saw the hill. (11) I remembered Coach Benally's words and shortened my steps. (12) I kept my eyes on the ground just ahead of my shoes. (13) I passed one runner and then another. (14) I reached the top and coasted down to the finish line.

(15) I finished the race.$q$, 'draft')
