  ('287884c7-4c50-549f-b3d3-9fc831c6419d', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g7-narrative-writing'), null, 'hard',
   $q$The writer wants sentence 7 to show clearly that the narrator ignored the advice in sentences 4 and 5. Which revision does this best?$q$, $q$[{"text":"I ran the first mile at a steady pace, exactly the way Coach Benally had told me to.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-later-events"},{"text":"I got caught up in the crowd, which was made up of runners from six different schools.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"},{"text":"I forgot every word of Coach Benally's advice and sprinted the first mile with the leaders.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Coach Benally changed her mind and shouted at me to sprint the first mile.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-sequence"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$I forgot every word of Coach Benally's advice and sprinted the first mile with the leaders.$q$, $q$The correct choice links the fast start to the forgotten advice, which explains why the narrator is tired in sentence 8. The steady pace choice contradicts the heavy legs and aching side that come next.$q$, 'draft', '77381ee9-bc59-5c9c-9357-3a5d3b4561be')
