   $q$Which revision of sentence 8 uses dialogue in a way that fits the events that follow?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Mr. Nakamura gave me some helpful advice about how to sit at the wheel.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"summary-not-dialogue"},{"text":"\"Push harder and use all of your strength,\" Mr. Nakamura said.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"dialogue-contradicts-events"},{"text":"\"Let the wheel do the work,\" I told Mr. Nakamura with a nod.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-speaker"},{"text":"\"Lock your elbows on your knees,\" Mr. Nakamura said. \"Let the wheel work.\"","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$"Lock your elbows on your knees," Mr. Nakamura said. "Let the wheel work."$q$, $q$The correct choice gives Mr. Nakamura's own words, and the next sentences show the narrator following them. The choice telling the narrator to push harder contradicts the story, since pushing harder is what failed in sentence 6.$q$, 'draft', '01a7b91b-2371-5f77-a4e9-ecf6f09af0f4')
