        '6-8', $q$How a Hot Air Balloon Flies$q$, $q$(1) A hot air balloon can float high above the ground without wings or a motor. (2) The secret is simple: warm air is lighter than cool air. (3) A burner under the balloon shoots a flame upward into the large fabric bag, called the envelope. (4) The flame heats the air trapped inside the envelope. (5) As that air warms, it spreads out and becomes less dense than the cooler air outside. (6) ____, the balloon begins to rise, lifting the basket and its passengers with it.

