   $q$Read the sentence: "The desert cactus stores water inside of its thick stem so that it can survive and live through long dry spells." Which revision is the most concise?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The cactus stores water inside of its stem to survive.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"drops-key-meaning"},{"text":"The desert cactus stores water inside its thick stem so it can survive and live through long dry spells.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"keeps-redundancy"},{"text":"The desert cactus stores water in its stem so that it is able to survive and live.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"keeps-redundancy"},{"text":"The desert cactus stores water in its thick stem to survive long dry spells.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The desert cactus stores water in its thick stem to survive long dry spells.$q$, $q$"Survive" and "live through" mean the same thing, and "in" works as well as "inside of." The choice "The desert cactus stores water inside its thick stem so it can survive and live through long dry spells" trims "of" but keeps "survive and live through."$q$, 'draft', null)
