   $q$Read the paragraph: "The printing press changed history. It changed history because books could be made faster. Before it existed, books were copied by hand, which was slow. Copying by hand took a long time." Which sentence should be deleted because it is redundant?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Copying by hand took a long time.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The printing press changed history.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"deletes-main-idea"},{"text":"Before it existed, books were copied by hand, which was slow.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"deletes-new-information"},{"text":"It changed history because books could be made faster.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"deletes-new-information"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Copying by hand took a long time.$q$, $q$"Before it existed, books were copied by hand, which was slow" already says hand copying was slow, so "Copying by hand took a long time" adds nothing new. "It changed history because books could be made faster" repeats "changed history," but it also gives the reason, which is new information.$q$, 'draft', null)
