   $q$Read the sentence: "It is my belief that it would be a good idea for the school to consider the possibility of adding a bike rack." Which revision is the most concise while keeping the writer's meaning?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The school is adding a bike rack.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"changes-meaning"},{"text":"I believe it would be a good idea for the school to consider adding a bike rack.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"keeps-wordiness"},{"text":"I think the school should consider adding a bike rack.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It is my belief that the school should consider the possibility of a bike rack.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"keeps-wordiness"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$I think the school should consider adding a bike rack.$q$, $q$"I think the school should consider adding a bike rack" keeps the writer's opinion and the suggestion in ten words. "The school is adding a bike rack" is short but turns a suggestion into a statement of fact.$q$, 'draft', null)
