   $q$Read the sentence: "The Mars rover moved across the surface of the planet, collecting rock samples from the ground of the red planet." Which revision is the most concise without losing meaning?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The rover moved around collecting samples.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"drops-key-meaning"},{"text":"The Mars rover crossed the planet's surface, collecting rock samples.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The Mars rover moved across the planet's surface, collecting rock samples from the ground of the planet.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"keeps-redundancy"},{"text":"Moving across the red planet's surface, the Mars rover collected rock samples from the red planet's ground.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"keeps-redundancy"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The Mars rover crossed the planet's surface, collecting rock samples.$q$, $q$Rock samples gathered while crossing the surface obviously come from the ground of Mars, so the last phrase repeats information. "The rover moved around collecting samples" drops which planet and what kind of samples.$q$, 'draft', null)
