   $q$Read the sentence: "The canal was finished in 1825, and its completion in that year allowed boats to carry goods west more cheaply than before." Which revision is the most concise?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The canal was completed and finished in 1825, letting boats carry goods west more cheaply.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"keeps-redundancy"},{"text":"The canal let boats carry goods.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"drops-key-meaning"},{"text":"The canal, finished in 1825, was completed that year and let boats carry goods cheaply.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"keeps-redundancy"},{"text":"Finished in 1825, the canal let boats carry goods west more cheaply.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Finished in 1825, the canal let boats carry goods west more cheaply.$q$, $q$The original says the canal was done in 1825 twice, once as "finished" and once as "its completion in that year." The choice "The canal was completed and finished in 1825, letting boats carry goods west more cheaply" still uses both "completed" and "finished."$q$, 'draft', null)
