   $q$Read the sentence: "When the snowstorm hit, the city sent out the trucks that clear snow from the roads to make the roads safe for drivers to use." Which revision is the most concise and precise?$q$, $q$[{"text":"When the storm hit, the city did things to make roads safe.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"vague-verb"},{"text":"When the snowstorm hit, the city sent out snowplows to clear the roads.","is_correct":true},{"text":"When the snowstorm hit, the city sent out some trucks for the roads.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"vague-noun"},{"text":"When the snowstorm hit, the city sent out trucks that clear snow to make the roads safe for drivers.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"keeps-wordiness"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$When the snowstorm hit, the city sent out snowplows to clear the roads.$q$, $q$"Snowplows" is the exact name for trucks that clear snow, which removes a whole clause. The choice "When the snowstorm hit, the city sent out trucks that clear snow to make the roads safe for drivers" trims a few words but still describes the trucks instead of naming them.$q$, 'draft', null)
